    "answer": {
      "short": "Both are correct. Translating $y=(x+1)^3$ right 2 units gives $y=(x-1)^3$; rotating it $180^\\circ$ about the origin gives the same graph.\n\nUse $x\\mapsto x-2$ for the translation and replace both $x$ and $y$ by their negatives for the rotation.",
      "worked": "Translate $y=(x+1)^3$ right 2 units by replacing $x$ by $x-2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x-2+1)^3\\\\y&=(x-1)^3\\end{align*}$$\nFor a $180^\\circ$ rotation about the origin, replace both $x$ and $y$ by their negatives:\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=(-x+1)^3\\\\-y&=-(x-1)^3\\\\y&=(x-1)^3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth Bob and Mary are correct.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
